# Auto-Deploy After Edits

After making any code or content changes to this project, automatically:

1. **Stage** all changes: `git add -A`
2. **Commit** with a descriptive message summarizing what was changed
3. **Push** to origin: `git push`

This triggers Netlify to deploy the updates. Do this at the end of the session when edits are complete — do not ask the user; just run the commands.

Use PowerShell-compatible syntax (e.g. `;` instead of `&&` for command chaining).
